      "updated_at": "2026-01-26T11:55:58Z",
      "body": "Usually Python code should not be able to cause SystemError. But this is a special case. This error happened in case of potential buffer overflow. Python cannot prevent it (unless we add a table for all `ioctl()` operation codes), it can only detect a misuse of the API post factum. There may be no stack or heap corruption (like in this particular example), but Python does not know this.",
