      "created_at": "2026-01-27T11:17:22Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-27T11:17:22Z",
      "body": "I misunderstood the issue. `fcntl.ioctl(fd, termios.TIOCGPGRP, b'', True)` misuses the `ioctl()` function which requires a `pid_t` (4 bytes), whereas the function is called with 0 bytes.\n\nI agree that raising a SystemError is the best we can do in this case. The alternative would be to trigger a fatal error.\n\nPython works as expected, and I don't think that anything else should be done, so I suggest closing the issue.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
