      "created_at": "2026-01-27T11:42:19Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-27T11:42:19Z",
      "body": "This is actually similar to #141338. Both are not real issues reported by users, but were found by a (semi-)automatic  random testing.\n\nI thought about it again and came to the conclusion that SystemError is the correct type of exception. This is very close to the C API misuse. Even if there is no memory corruption, another type of exception can be accidentally silenced.\n\nWhat can we do -- improve the error message. The benefit of the short error message is that it's generation will less likely fail if the memory corruption occurred, but currently it is not enough clear.",
